No memory writer in the fork is frontmatter-aware, and the identifier `modified` does not exist in the subsystem (`grep -ran modified packages/shared/src/agent/memory/ packages/session-tools-core/src/` -> zero hits; `-a` passed for the NUL-byte trap). There are exactly two writers, and both build the next file contents as plain string concatenation. (1) The agent-facing `remember` tool: `packages/session-tools-core/src/handlers/remember.ts:27-37` `formatMemoryFile` strips marker lookalikes, builds `- ${trimmed} ${autoMemoryMarker()}`, and either seeds `# Memory

${entry}
` for an empty file or returns `${existing.trimEnd()}

${entry}
`; `remember.ts:39-49` `appendMemory` writes that string via temp-file + rename at mode 0600. It is registered at `packages/session-tools-core/src/tool-defs.ts:981` (`{ name: 'remember', ... handler: handleRemember }`) and reached by `handleRemember` at `remember.ts:73-92`. (2) The UI/RPC path: `packages/shared/src/agent/memory/memory-store.ts:112-120` is the same `formatMemoryFile` minus the marker, and `memory-store.ts:122-132` `appendMemoryFile` performs the same atomic 0600 write; it is called at `packages/server-core/src/handlers/rpc/sessions.ts:80`, whose renderer trigger is the `type: 'appendMemory'` message at `apps/electron/src/renderer/components/app-shell/ChatDisplay.tsx:1557`. Neither writer reads the existing file's first line, parses a `---` block, or emits a timestamp of any kind at file scope. The third mutator, the scheduled sweep `cleanupAutoMemoryFile` (`packages/shared/src/agent/memory/memory-cleanup.ts:185-204`) and its pure core `cleanupAutoMemoryContent` (`memory-cleanup.ts:119-182`), is equally frontmatter-blind: it copies every unmarked line through byte-identically and only deletes marked entry lines, so an existing frontmatter block survives a sweep untouched and unstamped. The only per-write date Nessy records is the per-ENTRY marker `<!-- nessy:auto:YYYY-MM-DD -->` (`remember.ts:21-25`, regex source `AUTO_MEMORY_MARKER_REGEX_SOURCE` at `memory-store.ts:159`), and it is day-granular, attached to a bullet rather than the file, and deleted before the model sees it: `stripAutoMemoryMarkers` (`memory-store.ts:161-163`) runs inside `mergeMemoryContents` (`memory-store.ts:165-183`, strip at :173) on the load path `readMemoryFile` (`:29-33`) -> `readMemoryFileWithImports` (`:66-110`) -> `loadMemoryPromptBlock` (`:317-334`). The one frontmatter parser in the package, `parseRuleFile` (`memory-store.ts:214-262`), belongs to the sibling `.agents/rules` path-scoped-rules subsystem (`MEMORY_RULES_DIR` at `memory-store.ts:9`), is read-only, and recognises only `path`/`paths`/`glob`/`globs` (`:248`).
